---

<figure>
	<Image
		src={art}
		width={1400}
		alt="A user request goes to Classify, which routes it to the main LLM. Tool output passes through Compress before reaching the LLM. The agent trace goes to a second Classify that checks for looping and can stop the run. Documents go to Extract, which writes spans with offsets into your database."
		class="block h-auto w-full"
	/>
	<figcaption>Small models handle routing, shrinking and extraction. The general LLM handles what actually needs writing. The loop check comes from LangChain's example, which stops a run when Classify scores "looping" above 0.8.</figcaption>
</figure>
